---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '@/lib/site-config';
---

<BaseLayout title="Refunds & SLA Commitments | SimbNext" description="SLA commitments, guarantees, and service cancellation terms at SimbNext.">
  <!-- Light Header Section -->
  <div class="pt-36 pb-16 bg-gradient-to-b from-[#FFF2F5] via-[#FCF6F8] to-white text-[#0E090D] border-b border-[#F0DEE4]">
    <div class="container-wide max-w-3xl space-y-3">
      <span class="chip-synthesia">Governance & Compliance</span>
      <h1 class="headline-lg text-[#0E090D]">Refunds & SLA Terms</h1>
      <p class="text-xs text-[#7A636E] font-mono">Last updated: January 2026</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="py-16 bg-[#FFFFFF]">
    <div class="container-wide max-w-3xl prose prose-neutral text-sm space-y-6 text-[#3A2A33]">
      <p>
        At {SITE.legalName}, we operate on explicit Service Level Agreements (SLAs). Our engagement terms are designed to be completely transparent and fair.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-[#0E090D] mt-6">1. 14-Day Zero-Risk Pilot</h2>
      <p>
        New clients embarking on our initial pilot phase have a 14-day evaluation window. If our active Desks do not meet the agreed onboarding SLAs, we will address issues immediately or refund any upfront setup fee.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-[#0E090D] mt-6">2. Monthly Retainers</h2>
      <p>
        Because monthly retainers allocate dedicated specialist capacity, media management, and server infrastructure, monthly retainer fees are non-refundable once the monthly billing cycle has commenced.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-[#0E090D] mt-6">3. SLA Credits</h2>
      <p>
        In the rare event that a critical delivery SLA or uptime commitment is materially breached without prior notice, we provide service credits toward your next month's retainer.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
